  "task": {
    "id": "waste_segregation_mix_fault_v1_renamed",
    "name": "Waste Segregation Mix Fault",
    "output": "outputs/waste_segregation_mix_fault",
    "limitations": [
      "rigid constrained grasp and support proxies for all three containers; no pour, no cap, no seal",
      "the autoclave is the existing generic instrument: it reports load/run/unload lifecycle only, with no temperature curve, pressure or sterilisation assurance",
      "the hypochlorite soak is an accelerated wait; the logical 1800 s is recorded separately from physics time and no disinfection reaction is simulated",
      "the incompatible-mixture model is a declared component-coexistence inference from committed execution transitions; it does not model reaction products, heat, gas, pressure, severity or real chemical validation. A normal run keeping the streams apart does not prove every hazard is covered",
      "the autoclave load and outfeed poses are now checked, but only for this container (collision radius 11 mm, height 100 mm) against the instrument collision bounds and the raise/traverse/lower place path of sim/mechanisms/rigid_object.py; a taller or wider vessel, or a support added inside the tray footprint x [0.70, 0.86] y [-0.66, -0.54], needs the clearance measured again",
      "the container lands exactly on the autoclave tray top face (z 0.970), so instrument_load peaks at 11.9 N: over the 10 N soft limit, under the 40 N hard limit, meaning the arm is force-slowed on the way in. No approach offset or tray-height margin is modelled",
      "all volumes, the soak duration and the autoclave program duration are test values (parameters.test_values)",
      "the formal flow adds 500 uL of the 0.5 % hypochlorite stock (5000 ppm available chlorine) to 1000 uL of aqueous waste, a derived final concentration of about 1670 ppm; this is an engineering placeholder below the 5000 ppm that spec 3.12 requires, and no criterion checks the concentration"
    ]
  },
